o longer runs any test suite. Its own comment records that the suites that used to run there were report-only and moved to CI, so the push path is now structural gates only. [SOURCE: .skilled/scripts/git-hooks/pre-push:481]\n 5. The most expensive local check is the track-root sweep at 2.27s, and it runs once per pushed ref. It is pre-push only, so it adds about 2.3s to a push and nothing to a commit. [SOURCE: .skilled/scripts/git-hooks/pre-push:577]\n 6. The repository has no root `package.json` and `.skilled/package.json` declares no `scripts` block, so there is no single \"run the tests\" command. Suites are invoked per package, which is why no local aggregate suite cost exists to cut. [SOURCE: .skilled/package.json:1][SOURCE: .gitignore:1]\n 7. The hook path is therefore not the source of the operator's multi-minute waits: a commit costs about a second and a push about three seconds, while the cheapest measured CI workflow costs 10s and the most expensive 595s. The premise \"minutes on every commit\" is unsupported for hooks and should be dropped from the cut list. [SOURCE: specs/system-speckit/runtime-and-release/006-test-cycle-speed/007-test-and-ci-bloat-research/spec.md:82][SOURCE: specs/system-speckit/runtime-and-release/006-test-cycle-speed/007-test-and-ci-bloat-research/spec.md:113]\n","status":"modified","additions":1,"deletions":1}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-speckit/runtime-and-release/006-test-cycle-speed/007-test-and-ci-bloat-research/research/lineages/opencode-go/iterations/iteration-001.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \"specs/system-speckit/runtime-and-release/006-test-cycle-speed/007-test-and-ci-bloat-research/research/lineages/opencode-go/iterations/iteration-001.md\", \"oldString\": \"3. The commit hook pays for process startup rather than for checking: it spawns at least twelve `node` processes, and the measured per-pr