{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794469303507,"sessionID":"ses_e3154f688fferuJUyllFRey6r8","part":{"id":"prt_1ceb494d3001IJHh0eUg7aOkKX","sessionID":"ses_e3154f688fferuJUyllFRey6r8","messageID":"msg_1ceb48de1001vFPzI02l5ADjH3","type":"step-start","snapshot":"9a26b131a1f13ee3348f1297493c675bcc5940a3"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794469325434,"sessionID":"ses_e3154f688fferuJUyllFRey6r8","part":{"partID":"prt_1ceb4a634001bCuuyn1Saezr7a","sessionID":"ses_e3154f688fferuJUyllFRey6r8","messageID":"msg_1ceb48de1001vFPzI02l5ADjH3","type":"tool","id":"call_00_ez0onso99azetdwhnqprugts","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Iteration 5: Test files under specs/ — what runs, what does not, and what the census missed\n\n## Focus\n\nKey question 4: which test files under `specs/` guard retired or closed-packet code rather than shipping behavior. `spec.md` records \"about 110 under specs/ (most in specs/cli-classifier/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration)\" without saying whether any of them run. This iteration establishes the tracked count, the execution path, and whether the census itself is complete.\n\n## Actions Taken\n\n1. Counted test files under `specs/` with `node_modules` pruned, then grouped them by packet.\n2. Recounted against the git index only, to separate tracked files from untracked context trees.\n3. Searched every vitest config and every workflow for a collector that includes `specs/**`.\n4. Measured the largest untracked context tree and checked whether git tracks it.\n5. Counted lines across the tracked set.\n\n## Findings\n\n1. The tracked test surface under `specs/` is 94 files and 53,629 lines, not \"about 110\". The difference matters because every later count in this packet must be compared against a tracked file list, not a filesystem walk. [SOURCE: specs/system-speckit/runtime-and-release/006-test-cycle-speed/007-test-and-ci-bloat-research/spec.md:111]\n2. 77 of the 94 tracked files (82%) live in one packet, `specs/cli-classifier/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration`; the remaining 17 are spread across six packets, and `specs/sk-code/hub-architecture` holds seven of them. [SOURCE: specs/cli-classifier/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/007-classifier-deep-research/context/deem-main/docs/MODEL_CARD_8B.md:1]\n3. No runner collects them: no `vitest.config.*` in the repository includes a `specs/` glob, and no workflow runs a `specs/` test path. They cost zero CI minutes today. [SOURCE: .skilled/vitest.config.bin.ts:7][SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/vitest.config.ts:18]\n4. Because they never run, deleting them saves no run time. The honest label for this set is \"move out of the test surface\", not \"delete bloat\", and a ranked cut list that prices them in minutes would be wrong. [INFERENCE: based on the absence of any collector in finding 3 and the 94-file tracked count in finding 1]\n5. The census in `spec.md` undercounts the filesystem by two orders of magnitude if untracked context is included: 9,869 test files exist under `specs/`, and the bulk sit in one vendored tree. [SOURCE: specs/system-speckit/runtime-and-release/006-test-cycle-speed/007-test-and-ci-bloat-research/spec.md:111]\n6. That vendored tree, `specs/cli-orca/002-consolidate-official-orca-skills/context/orca-main`, is 292 MB and untracked — `git ls-files` returns nothing for it. It costs disk and editor indexing, not CI time, so it belongs in a workspace-weight finding rather than a run-time finding. [INFERENCE: based on `git ls-files` returning 0 paths and `du -sh` reporting 292M]\n7. Four tracked test files sit under `specs/*/z_archive`, a directory the packet convention treats as retired history. They are the only files in the set that are unambiguously guarding nothing. [SOURCE: specs/system-speckit/runtime-and-release/006-test-cycle-speed/007-test-and-ci-bloat-research/spec.md:136]\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- Pricing a `specs/` test deletion as a run-time saving: there is no execution path, so the saving is 0 minutes and claiming otherwise would inflate the ranking.\n- Recommending that these 94 files be wired into CI so they \"earn their keep\": that would add run time to a packet whose purpose is to remove it, and the files were written as packet evidence, not as a regression suite.\n- Deleting the 292 MB orca context tree as a test-bloat cut: it is untracked working material, not a test surface, and deleting another packet's context is outside this research scope.\n\n## Dead Ends\n\n- Searching for a hidden runner by name (`cli-jev-workflow-integration`) found only benchmark scripts and fixture indices that reference packet paths as data, never a test command. No collection path exists.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- Ambiguous input: \"test files under specs/\" could mean tracked files or every file on disk. Selected interpretation: tracked files, because only tracked files are part of the repository and only they can gate a change. Deferred alternative: the untracked corpus, reported separately as finding 6.\n- Contradictory evidence: `spec.md` says about 110 files, the tracker says 94, and the filesystem says 9,869. All three can be true at once; the finding names which measure is which rather than choosing one.\n- Missing dependencies: none.\n- Partial success: none.\n\n## SCOPE VIOLATIONS\n\nNone. Every write in this iteration is inside the lineage directory.\n\n## Sources Consulted\n\n- `specs/system-speckit/runtime-and-release/006-test-cycle-speed/007-test-and-ci-bloat-research/spec.md:111`\n- `specs/cli-classifier/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/007-classifier-deep-research/context/deem-main/docs/MODEL_CARD_8B.md:1`\n- `.skilled/vitest.config.bin.ts:7`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/vitest.config.ts:18`\n- Measured: 94 tracked `specs/` test files / 53,629 lines; 9,869 files on disk; `specs/cli-orca/.../context/orca-main` = 292 MB with 0 tracked paths.\n\n## Assessment\n\n- New information ratio: 1.0\n- Questions addressed: Which test files under specs/ guard retired or closed-packet code rather than shipping behavior?\n- Questions answered: Which test files under specs/ guard retired or closed-packet code rather than shipping behavior?\n\n## Reflection\n\n- What worked and why: comparing three different counts (spec prose, git index, filesystem) exposed that the census mixed measures, and the git index gave the only number that can gate a change.\n- What did not work and why: the expected finding — \"110 unrun test files cost maintenance\" — is not a run-time finding at all; the execution-path search is what converted it into an honest zero.\n- What I would do differently: check for a collector before counting files in any next tree, because file counts without an execution path cannot be priced in minutes.\n\n## Recommended Next Focus\n\nThe `specs/cli-classifier/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration` packet holds 77 unrun test files and a large benchmark surface; check whether its tests duplicate assertions already made by the classifier's shipping runtime suite under `.skilled/skills/cli-classifier`, and whether the packet is open or closed.\n","path":"specs/system-speckit/runtime-and-release/006-test-cycle-speed/007-test-and-ci-bloat-research/research/lineages/opencode-go/iterations/iteration-005.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-speckit/runtime-and-release/006-test-cycle-speed/007-test-and-ci-bloat-research/research/lineages/opencode-go/iterations/iteration-005.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-speckit/runtime-and-release/006-test-cycle-speed/007-test-and-ci-bloat-research/research/lineages/opencode-go/iterations/iteration-005.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"# Iteration 5: Test files under specs/ — what runs, what does not, and what the census missed\\n\\n## Focus\\n\\nKey question 4: which test files under `specs/` guard retired or closed-packet code rather than shipping behavior. `spec.md` records \\\"about 110 under specs/ (most in specs/cli-classifier/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration)\\\" without saying whether any of them run. This iteration establishes the tracked count, the execution path, and whether the census itself is complete.\\n\\n## Actions Taken\\n\\n1. Counted test files under `specs/` with `node_modules` pruned, then grouped them by packet.\\n2. Recounted against the git index only, to separate tracked files from untracked context trees.\\n3. Searched every vitest config and every workflow for a collector that includes `specs/**`.\\n4. Measured the largest untracked context tree and checked whether git tracks it.\\n5. Counted lines across the tracked set.\\n\\n## Findings\\n\\n1. The tracked test surface under `specs/` is 94 files and 53,629 lines, not \\\"about 110\\\". The difference matters because every later count in this packet must be compared against a tracked file list, not a filesystem walk. [SOURCE: specs/system-speckit/runtime-and-release/006-test-cycle-speed/007-test-and-ci-bloat-research/spec.md:111]\\n2. 77 of the 94 tracked files (82%) live in one packet, `specs/cli-classifier/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration`; the remaining 17 are spread across six packets, and `specs/sk-code/hub-architecture` holds seven of them. [SOURCE: specs/cli-classifier/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/007-classifier-deep-research/context/deem-main/docs/MODEL_CARD_8B.md:1]\\n3. No runner collects them: no `vitest.config.*` in the repository includes a `specs/` glob, and no workflow runs a `specs/` test path. They cost zero CI minutes today. [SOURCE: .skilled/vitest.config.bin.ts:7][SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/vitest.config.ts:18]\\n4. Because they never run, deleting them saves no run time. The honest label for this set is \\\"move out of the test surface\\\", not \\\"delete bloat\\\", and a ranked cut list that prices them in minutes would be wrong. [INFERENCE: based on the absence of any collector in finding 3 and the 94-file tracked count in finding 1]\\n5. The census in `spec.md` undercounts the filesystem by two orders of magnitude if untracked context is included: 9,869 test files exist under `specs/`, and the bulk sit in one vendored tree. [SOURCE: specs/system-speckit/runtime-and-release/006-test-cycle-speed/007-test-and-ci-bloat-research/spec.md:111]\\n6. That vendored tree, `specs/cli-orca/002-consolidate-official-orca-skills/context/orca-main`, is 292 MB and untracked — `git ls-files` returns nothing for it. It costs disk and editor indexing, not CI time, so it belongs in a workspace-weight finding rather than a run-time finding. [INFERENCE: based on `git ls-files` returning 0 paths and `du -sh` reporting 292M]\\n7. Four tracked test files sit under `specs/*/z_archive`, a directory the packet convention treats as retired history. They are the only files in the set that are unambiguously guarding nothing. [SOURCE: specs/system-speckit/runtime-and-release/006-test-cycle-speed/007-test-and-ci-bloat-research/spec.md:136]\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- Pricing a `specs/` test deletion as a run-time saving: there is no execution path, so the saving is 0 minutes and claiming otherwise would inflate the ranking.\\n- Recommending that these 94 files be wired into CI so they \\\"earn their keep\\\": that would add run time to a packet whose purpose is to remove it, and the files were written as packet evidence, not as a regression suite.\\n- Deleting the 292 MB orca context tree as a test-bloat cut: it is untracked working material, not a test surface, and deleting another packet's context is outside this research scope.\\n\\n## Dead Ends\\n\\n- Searching for a hidden runner by name (`cli-jev-workflow-integration`) found only benchmark scripts and fixture indices that reference packet paths as data, never a test command. No collection path exists.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- Ambiguous input: \\\"test files under specs/\\\" could mean tracked files or every file on disk. Selected interpretation: tracked files, because only tracked files are part of the repository and only they can gate a change. Deferred alternative: the untracked corpus, reported separately as finding 6.\\n- Contradictory evidence: `spec.md` says about 110 files, the tracker says 94, and the filesystem says 9,869. All three can be true at once; the finding names which measure is which rather than choosing one.\\n- Missing dependencies: none.\\n- Partial success: none.\\n\\n## SCOPE VIOLATIONS\\n\\nNone. Every write in this iteration is inside the lineage directory.\\n\\n## Sources Consulted\\n\\n- `specs/system-speckit/runtime-and-release/006-test-cycle-speed/007-test-and-ci-bloat-research/spec.md:111`\\n- `specs/cli-classifier/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/007-classifier-deep-research/context/deem-main/docs/MODEL_CARD_8B.md:1`\\n- `.skilled/vitest.config.bin.ts:7`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/vitest.config.ts:18`\\n- Measured: 94 tracked `specs/` test files / 53,629 lines; 9,869 files on disk; `specs/cli-orca/.../context/orca-main` = 292 MB with 0 tracked paths.\\n\\n## Assessment\\n\\n- New information ratio: 1.0\\n- Questions addressed: Which test files under specs/ guard retired or closed-packet code rather than shipping behavior?\\n- Questions answered: Which test files under specs/ guard retired or closed-packet code rather than shipping behavior?\\n\\n## Reflection\\n\\n- What worked and why: comparing three different counts (spec prose, git index, filesystem) exposed that the census mixed measures, and the git index gave the only number that can gate a change.\\n- What did not work and why: the expected finding — \\\"110 unrun test files cost maintenance\\\" — is not a run-time finding at all; the execution-path search is what converted it into an honest zero.\\n- What I would do differently: check for a collector before counting files in any next tree, because file counts without an execution path cannot be priced in minutes.\\n\\n## Recommended Next Focus\\n\\nThe `specs/cli-classifier/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration` packet holds 77 unrun test files and a large benchmark surface; check whether its tests duplicate assertions already made by the classifier's shipping runtime suite under `.skilled/skills/cli-classifier`, and whether the packet is open or closed.\\n\", \"path\": \"specs/system-speckit/runtime-and-release/006-test-cycle-speed/007-test-and-ci-bloat-research/research/lineages/opencode-go/iterations/iteration-005.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794469307956,"end":1794469325434}}}}
