{"type":"text","timestamp":1794469866369,"sessionID":"ses_e3154f688fferuJUyllFRey6r8","part":{"id":"prt_1cebd1ee1003IiaEU3f1O7EPfR","sessionID":"ses_e3154f688fferuJUyllFRey6r8","messageID":"msg_1cebd117b001q76KIZvkouH13l","type":"text","text":"Lineage complete. Summary of what ran and what it found:\n\n**Execution** — 10 iterations, each with an iteration narrative, a delta JSONL, one iteration record through `append-mode-event.cjs` (ledger sequences 2–11), and `reduce-state.cjs` after every iteration. Terminal `synthesis_complete` record carries `stopReason: maxIterationsReached`; config status is `complete`.\n\n**Findings worth the operator's attention**\n- **Hooks are not the problem.** Commit ≈ 1s (12 node startups), push ≈ 3s (track sweep 2.27s is the costliest check). Every measured hook checker is ≤ 0.13s.\n- **Four CI workflows re-run a guard that already blocks locally**, worth 385s per PR measured from `gh run view`: `comment-hygiene` 92s, `naming-standard-guard` 88s, `agent-mirror-sync` 85s, plus up to 120s of `routing-registry-drift`. `main` has no branch protection, so none is a required check.\n- **The largest real costs** are the spec-kit CLI Vitest project (490s), advisor default suite (309s) and deep-loop suite (306s) — actual work, no defensible cut found.\n- **The packet census is wrong about `specs/`**: 94 tracked test-suffixed files, 86 of them `scratch/` build logs, 2 fixtures, 4 archived, only 4 real tests, and no runner collects any of them.\n- **Second-tier workflows can't be cut at the check level** — checks are 10–66s against 96–188s of checkout plus install; that ceiling is the settled caching/trigger work.\n\n**Verification status** — confirmed by command: checker-file identity for the duplicate guards, zero `test:sharded` callers, 3,561 legacy-lane lines, 1,173 + 94 census, no branch protection, all quoted run durations. Inferred and named as measurement gates: the legacy lane's 161s ceiling and advisor parallel safety.\n\n**Caveats, stated rather than hidden** — iteration 1's immutable ledger record says `findingsCount: 5` while 7 findings were enumerated; re-appending would duplicate the iteration, so the count stands and the discrepancy is documented in iteration 2 and in `research.md`. The gate-3 writeback into the packet's `spec.md` and `validate.sh` were deliberately skipped because they fall outside this lineage's write surface. A concurrent session is modifying unrelated tracked files (`AGENTS.md`, repo-rules, sk-doc experiment scripts); none of those edits are mine — every write in this lineage landed under `research/lineages/opencode-go/`.\n\nFANOUT_LINEAGE_COMPLETE:opencode-go","time":{"start":1794469863137,"end":1794469866369}}}
